rac{1}{\\sin x} = \\csc x,$ we can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we see that this is just a standard trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2x}\\,\\textrm d x  =  \\int\\csc^2 x\\,\\textrm d x =-\\cot x + C\n$$\n\nWhen confronted with a tricky-looking trigonometric integral, we can often reduce it to a standard integral using a trigonometric identity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065435 #edb/ref 1065 867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065435 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d2dcb6a2-e8f7-5bb7-9450-e0b65532681a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065435 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247760 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247760 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247760 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2621a51d-6ea2-5c0c-b0e8-ef9a5309fa09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248353 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248353 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248353 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "679c8c73-db45-58a5-8311-c18d1aa796b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248924 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248924 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248924 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8bb94e3-7ab2-5067-a9f7-907364396e08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249242 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc6ee47a-69b2-58b2-804c-4404e96412f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186249410 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C